<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns two secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns two secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has assigned the first two of five auctions whereby it sought to drain 4.426 billion pesos from the secondary market.</p>
<p>The auctions were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>CREDIT AUCTIONS    TERM     MAX    MIN     AVERAGE  BIDS BIDDERS</p>
<p>700 million pesos 16 days  23.83  23.82     23.83    3     3</p>
<p>900 million pesos  9 days  23.69  23.60     23.64    4     4</p>
<p>1.500 bln pesos    3 days</p>
<p>900 million pesos  2 days</p>
<p>426 million pesos  1 day</p>
<p>NOTE - The maximum, minimum and average are percentages.</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9500))</p>
</text>
